[109.127775, "o", "    \"\"\"Compute the credit and charge for moving ``sub`` to ``new_plan_id`` on ``change_at``.\"\"\"\r\n    if new_plan_id == sub.plan_id:\r\n        raise ValueError(\"subscription is already on that plan\")\r\n    old = catalog.plan(sub.plan_id)\r\n    new = catalog.plan(new_plan_id)\r\n    if old.currency != new.currency:\r\n        raise ValueError(\"cross-currency plan changes are not supported\")\r\n\r\n    start, end = cycle_bounds(sub.anchor, change_at, old.interval)\r\n    period_days = days_between(start, end)\r\n    remaining = days_between(change_at, end)\r\n\r\n    credit = portion(catalog.price(old.plan_id, start), remaining, period_days)\r\n    new_price = catalog.price(new.plan_id, change_at)\r\n    if old.interval == new.interval:\r\n        charge = portion(new_price, remaining, period_days)\r\n        new_anchor = sub.anchor\r\n        next_renewal = end\r\n        charge_description = \"Remaining time\"\r\n    else:\r\n        charge = new_price\r\n        new_anchor = change_at\r\n        next_renewal = add_months(new_anchor, interval_months("]
[109.12781, "o", "new.interval))\r\n        charge_description = \"Full cycle\"\r\n\r\n\r\n    lines = [\r\n        Line(\"credit\", old.plan_id, -credit, change_at, end,\r\n             f\"Unused time on {old.name} ({change_at} to {end})\"),\r\n        Line(\"charge\", new.plan_id, charge, change_at, next_renewal,\r\n             f\"{charge_description} on {new.name} ({change_at} to {next_renewal})\"),\r\n    ]\r\n    return Proration(sub.sub_id, change_at, start, end, credit, charge,\r\n                     new_anchor, next_renewal, lines)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef renewal_after(sub: Subscription, on: date, catalog: Catalog) -> date:\r\n    \"\"\"Next renewal date strictly after ``on`` for an unchanged subscription.\"\"\"\r\n    plan = catalog.plan(sub.plan_id)\r\n    _, end = cycle_bounds(sub.anchor, on, plan.interval)\r\n    return end\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[109.128109, "o", "def renewal_schedule(sub: Subscription, count: int, catalog: Catalog) -> List[date]:\r\n    plan = catalog.plan(sub.plan_id)\r\n    return [add_months(sub.anchor, plan.months * k) for k in range(1, count + 1)]\r\n\u001b[?2004h"]
[109.128182, "o", "root@7812b4850765:/app# "]
[123.982576, "i", "python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('billing/proration.py')\np.write_text(p.read_text().replace('        charge_description = \"Full cycle\"\\n\\n\\n', '        charge_description = \"Full cycle\"\\n\\n'))\nPY\ncat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\n# BILL-212 implementation summary\n\nFixed in `billing/calendar.py` and `billing/proration.py`:\n\n- Month arithmetic now clamps to the target month's last day, not always day 28.\n- Every renewal is calculated from the original anchor, restoring month-end and\n  February 29 anchors after shorter months or non-leap years.\n- Proration uses actual cycle days and the old price effective at cycle start.\n- Same-interval changes retain the anchor; interval switches charge the full new\n  price and re-anchor on the change date, with matching invoice line periods.\n- Half-even rounding is applied once to an exact rational, independent of the\n  Decimal precision context. Public function signatures are unchanged.\n\nValidation: all finance worked examples pass, as do eight added re"]
[123.983005, "i", "gression tests\ncovering renewal boundaries, exact rounding, line periods, balances, leap-day\ninterval switches, and CLI previews for every worked example.\n\n## Release blocker: missing partner contract data\n\nThe full suite still reports one pre-existing error in\n`PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines`: `KeyError: 'P-31'`.\n`data/subscriptions.json` assigns `sub_1151` to P-31, but\n`data/partners.json` contains only P-12, P-17, and P-24. No authoritative P-31\ncommission rate is provided. Financial data and existing tests were left intact;\nno rate was invented and no test was skipped or weakened.\n\nFinance must supply the contracted P-31 rate (or confirm a correction to the\nsubscription's partner assignment). Then rerun:\n\n    cd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests\n\nDo not ship until the full suite is green.\nEOF\npython -m billing preview --sub data/subscriptions.json --id sub_1042 --to team-monthly --at 2026-03-10 --json\n"]
[123.983791, "o", "python - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[123.984049, "o", "from pathlib import Path\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> p = Path('billing/proration.py')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> p.write_text(p.read_text().replace('        charge_description = \"Full cycle\"\\n\\n\\n', '        charge_description = \"Full cycle\"\\n\\n'))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[123.985224, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> PY\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[124.004826, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@7812b4850765:/app# "]
[124.006914, "o", "cat > docs/BILL-212-summary.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # BILL-212 implementation summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Fixed in `billing/calendar.py` and `billing/proration.py`:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Month arithmetic now clamps to the target month's last day, not always day 28.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Every renewal is calculated from the original anchor, restoring month-end and\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   February 29 anchors after shorter months or non-leap years.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Proration uses actual cycle days and the old price effective at cycle start.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Same-interval changes retain the anchor; interval switches charge the full new\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   price and re-anchor on the change date, with matching invoice line periods.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - Half-even rounding is applied once to an exact rational, independent of the\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>   Decimal precision context. Public function signatures are unchanged.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>"]
[124.006939, "o", " Validation: all finance worked examples pass, as do eight added regression tests\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> covering renewal boundaries, exact rounding, line periods, balances, leap-day\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> interval switches, and CLI previews for every worked example.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## Release blocker: missing partner contract data\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> The full suite still reports one pre-existing error in\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `PartnerInvoiceTest.test_partner_commission_lines`: `KeyError: 'P-31'`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `data/subscriptions.json` assigns `sub_1151` to P-31, but\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> `data/partners.json` contains only P-12, P-17, and P-24. No authoritative P-31\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> commission rate is provided. Financial data and existing tests were left intact;\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> no rate was invented and no test was skipped or weakened.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Finance must supply the contracted P-31 rate (or confirm a correction to the\r\n\u001b[?2004l"]
[124.006945, "o", "\r\u001b[?2004h> subscription's partner assignment). Then rerun:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>     cd /app && python -m unittest discover -s tests\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Do not ship until the full suite is green.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[124.008079, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[124.008143, "o", "root@7812b4850765:/app# "]
